                <pb facs="0587" n="497" sameAs="frus:frus1918Russiav02/pg497"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 861.00/2304</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul at Archangel</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Cole</hi>)
                        <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Archangel</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1918-07-15T21:00:00+04:31"><hi rendition="#italic">July 15, 1918,
                                9 p.m.</hi></date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received July 20, 12.08 p.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>77. The attitude of the inhabitants of Archangel in anticipation of the arrival
                    of the Allied forces as follows: (1) Welcome on the part of civilians; (2)
                    publicly expressed disfavor toward military intervention by the local Bolshevik
                    leaders goaded thereto by Moscow; (3) part of the Archangel executive department
                    would nevertheless eventually cooperate as well as welcome the Allies, if they
                    proceed with tact, luring rather than bullying.</p>
                <p>My cipher telegrams in Russia will not be accepted except diplomatics to the
                    Department.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Cole</hi></signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
